From 6db84e6ae3a9125f80845cb0868b730111a868bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 13:34:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] DOS-PORT: GUS PCM path -- backend-dependent format +
 model-B SDL_INIT_AUDIO skip

Two of the same-session S5 GUS architecture's own findings, fixed
together since both are the direct consequence of the rig's PGGUS
profile having no simultaneous SB PCM device:

Gap 1 fix (sys_main.cpp): sys_audio_init() used to attempt
SDL_InitSubSystem(SDL_INIT_AUDIO) + dos_audio_mixer_init()'s SB-device
open unconditionally, then tear the WHOLE audio subsystem back down on
failure -- silencing dos_midi_backend_cold_init()'s own work too, not
just PCM. GUS now takes its own branch that never attempts SDL_INIT_AUDIO
at all (doskutsu's own "model B, out-of-band" shape). Also bridges the
operator's real ULTRASND/ULTRADIR env vars into the SDL hints
SDL_DOSGusInit() actually reads (mirrors doskutsu's own main.cpp bridge)
-- without this, GF1 detection fails closed unconditionally regardless
of whether real/emulated hardware is present, found the hard way testing
this same patch under DOSBox-X with GUS emulation enabled.

Correction #1 fix (dos_audio_mixer.{h,cpp}, sdldecoder.{h,cpp}): GUS PCM
is hard-locked to 8-bit unsigned (the only real-hardware-confirmed-safe
GF1 DMA upload path is 8-bit-only) while SB stays 16-bit signed -- the
single compile-time DOS_AUDIO_MIXER_FORMAT constant becomes
dos_audio_mixer_format(), resolved once from SDL_HINT_DOS_AUDIO_BACKEND.
sdldecoder.cpp now converts its own always-16-bit intermediate to
whichever format is actually active, once at Open() (dossage's own 0039
lesson: never per-chunk); its move constructor moves the new _pcmDevice
member too (a real gap found in review -- a moved-to decoder would
otherwise report _opened=true against an empty buffer). Under GUS,
dos_audio_mixer's own internal shape changes too, not just the format:
each voice wraps a shared/audio/gus_pcm_stream instance (its own
independent GF1 hardware voice) instead of a software ring -- no
software mixdown loop, the GF1 mixes multiple hardware voices itself.
The PUBLIC dos_audio_mixer API is unchanged; OpenAlSource never needs to
know which backend is active.

CMakeLists.txt: adds gus_sink.c/gus_pcm_stream.c as compiled sources
(same target_sources treatment midi_sched.c/opl3_sink.c/
waveblaster_sink.c already get).

See dosags PLAN.md's "S5 GUS architecture" section (Gap 1, "Correction
#1", "Correction #2") for the full research trail this rests on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
